#: ../../../prop_sf/RULE_PATTERNS.rst:2
msgid "<RULE>_PATTERNS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_sf/RULE_PATTERNS.rst:6
msgid "Patterns specification for instantiating the rule ``<RULE>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_sf/RULE_PATTERNS.rst:8
msgid ""
"The ``<RULE>_PATTERNS`` property may be set to a :ref:`semicolon-separated "
"list <CMake Language Lists>` of patterns using the syntax ``PATTERN=VALUE`` "
"or ``PATTERN=``. More precisely, each item must match the regular expression "
"``(^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+)=(.*)$``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_sf/RULE_PATTERNS.rst:13
msgid ""
"CMake will automatically drop any patterns which do not match against this "
"regular expression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_sf/RULE_PATTERNS.rst:16
msgid ""
"The expansion of patterns is done recursively at generation time so the "
"value of a pattern can refer any other pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_sf/RULE_PATTERNS.rst:20
msgid "Related properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_sf/RULE_PATTERNS.rst:22
msgid ":prop_fs:`RULE_PATTERNS` to specify patterns for a file set."
msgstr ""

